Compile ore D3D11 shader modules with D3DCOMPILE_OPTIMIZATION_LEVEL1.

- source/renderer/ore/d3d11/ore_shader_module_d3d11.cpp: Ore D3D11 shader modules compile with D3DCOMPILE_OPTIMIZATION_LEVEL1 (the fxc default, the level Rive's own D3D pipeline manager uses) instead of LEVEL3: D3DCompile at level 3 takes tens of seconds on the large lighting shaders of yup_renderer, and the driver optimizes the DXBC again anyway

diff --git a/source/renderer/ore/d3d11/ore_shader_module_d3d11.cpp b/source/renderer/ore/d3d11/ore_shader_module_d3d11.cpp
index 9566d735050c824ae1363f20597aef37be3f7157..9b5c3a30b0c261d379369d1bc3eb5cc34ded4aef 100644
--- a/source/renderer/ore/d3d11/ore_shader_module_d3d11.cpp
+++ b/source/renderer/ore/d3d11/ore_shader_module_d3d11.cpp
@@ -43,7 +43,7 @@ void ShaderModuleD3D11::ensureD3DShadersImpl(
       nullptr,
       entry,
       target,
-      D3DCOMPILE_ENABLE_STRICTNESS | D3DCOMPILE_OPTIMIZATION_LEVEL3,
+      D3DCOMPILE_ENABLE_STRICTNESS | D3DCOMPILE_OPTIMIZATION_LEVEL1,
       0,
       compiledBlob.GetAddressOf(),
